.TH HI 1
.SH NAME
hi \- local-first terminal AI assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hi
.RI [ PROMPT ]
.br
.B hi
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hi
is a terminal AI assistant that chats with a configured AI provider, remembers
conversations across sessions, and can act on the system through approved
tools. The assistant may propose terminal commands, read, write, search, list,
and delete files; every action is shown with a preview and risk level and runs
only after approval under the configured policy.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B hi PROMPT
Ask a single question and print the response without starting a chat.
.TP
.B hi chat
Start a new chat session.
.BR "\-\-session " ID
continues an existing one.
.TP
.B hi sessions
List saved sessions.
.TP
.B hi resume ID
Resume a saved session.
.TP
.B hi delete ID
Delete a saved session.
.B hi delete --all
deletes every session.
.TP
.B hi config
Run the interactive provider setup wizard.
.TP
.B hi doctor
Check local configuration and provider connectivity.
.TP
.B hi models
List the models exposed by the configured provider.
.TP
.B hi completions SHELL
Generate a completion script for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell.
.SH SLASH COMMANDS
Within a chat, /help [command], /sessions, /resume, /clear, /reset, /model,
/config, /doctor, /new, and /quit are handled locally and never sent to the
provider. Type "/" and press Tab to autocomplete.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HI_API_KEY
API key for the selected provider (overrides the config file).
.TP
.B HI_BASE_URL
Provider endpoint, e.g. https://api.openai.com/v1.
.TP
.B HI_MODEL
Model identifier.
.TP
.B HI_APPROVAL_MODE
always, safe-only, or never.
.SH FILES
.IP ~/.config/hi/config.env
Provider configuration. API keys are stored in the operating system credential store and a protected 0600 fallback file.
.IP ~/.local/share/hi/sessions.db
Local conversation database.
.SH SEE ALSO
The online documentation at <https://github.com/britonmearsty/hi>.